क॑श m. a kind of gnawing animal, a whip;
 f. कशा whip,
rope, rein.

काशिक a. coming from Kāśi or Benares;
 f. आ the town of
Benares (±वृत्ति T. of a commentary).

कश्मल f. ई & आ dirty,—foul;
 timid, shy. n. dirt;
timidity, shyness (also m.).

काश्मीर f. ई pertaining to or coming from Kaśmīra;
 m. =
कश्मीर.

कश्य॑प a. black toothed. m. tortoise;
 a class of divine
beings;
 N. of sev. Ṛṣis.

काश् काशते (काश˚ति) pp. काशित be visible, appear,
shine, be brilliant or pleasant. I. चा॑कशीति & चाकश्य॑ते shine
bright;
 see clearly, survey. — अभि I. shine bright upon, illumine;
look on, survey. अव be visible, lie open. निस् C निष्काशयति v.
कस्। प्र be visible, shine, radiate, appear, become clear or manifest.
C. प्रकाशयति (˚ते) make visible, cause to appear, show, unveil,
explain, declare as (acc.). संप्र & C. the same. वि appear. C.
display, spread;
 illuminate, irradiate. l. pp. विचा॑कशत् shining,
beaming;
 beholding, perceiving. सम् appear, behold.

कषाय a. astringent, sharp (of taste), fragrant, red,
dark-red. m. red colour, passion, emotion;
 decoct, extract, ointment
(also n.);
 n. a yellowish-red garment.

काषाय a. dyed brown-red;
 f. ई a kind of wasp or bee;
 n.
a brown-red garment.

काशि॑ m. the clenched hand or a handful;
 m. N. of a people;
काशि or काशी f. the town of Benares.

का॑ष्ठा f. race-course, course (esp. of the winds and
clouds);
 mark, goal, limit;
 summit, top, height (fig.);
 cardinal point
or quarter of the heaven;
 a cert. measure of time.
